  "type": "PARENT",
  "data": {
    "body": "A box contains machinery that can rotate. The total mass of the box plus the machinery is \\textbf{M} = 3.0 \\textbf{kg}. A string wound around the machinery comes through a small hole in the top of the box. Initially the box sits on the ground, and the machinery inside is not rotating (left figure). Then you pull upward on  the string with a force of constant magnitude \\textbf{F} = 120 \\textbf{N}. At an instant when you have pulled the string through a vertical distance \\textbf{d} = 0.80 \\textbf{m} out of the box (indicated on the right figure), the box has risen a height \\textbf{h} = 0.13 \\textbf{m} and the machinery inside is rotating. Answer the questions below for the instant shown in the right figure. Assume that the magnitude of acceleration due to gravity is \\textbf{g = 10} $m/s^2$",
    "numberingType": "NUMBER",
    "answerChoices": []
  },
